From 94080e5f4b1249208723ceef4786362383b97f66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Book Buddy Dev <dev@bookbuddy.local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 04:21:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: tap-to-open pack animation for author card reveal

Replaces the static reveal modal with a real unpacking moment:

- app/globals.css: card-pack-idle / card-pack-idle-legendary glow
  keyframes (rarity-themed pulsing box-shadow on the sealed pack),
  card-pack-sparkle-burst for drifting sparkle decorations, and a
  standard flip-card setup (card-flip-scene/card-flip-card/card-flip-face)
  using perspective + backface-visibility rather than a new animation
  library. Follows the same naming/structure as the existing landing-*
  keyframes, including a prefers-reduced-motion override.

- components/kids/ShelfClient.tsx: the reveal modal now opens sealed
  (a gift-box icon on a glowing gradient card themed by rarity) and
  flips to the revealed card on tap via a new packOpened state + openPack
  handler. Confetti now fires at the moment of opening the pack instead
  of the moment the API response arrives, so the celebration lines up
  with what the kid is looking at. Legendary/rare/common each get a
  differently-sized confetti burst.

No schema changes in this commit -- if cards aren't dropping/showing at
all, that's 014_author_cards.sql not having been run yet, not this.
